From: Tilo <tilo@tilo.so>
Subject: arm64: dts: qcom: x1e80100-lenovo-yoga-slim7x: reserve a ramoops region

The Yoga Slim 7x has reset itself with no kernel message in the journal,
because journald writes to disk only every few minutes and a reset takes
the unwritten tail with it. A RAM region the kernel never maps survives a
warm reset, so pstore can keep the console log and any oops or panic
dump there and hand them to the next boot.

Firmware does not describe such a region, and the low 4 GiB are full of
firmware carve-outs. The region sits in the middle of the high bank, away
from the top, where the boot loader and the EFI stub allocate, and from
the bottom, where the firmware's runtime regions sit. Error correction
lets ramoops recover a record a boot-time allocation only partly
overwrote.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-lenovo-yoga-slim7x.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-lenovo-yoga-slim7x.dts
index 9eb2dfd..ad5b87e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-lenovo-yoga-slim7x.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-lenovo-yoga-slim7x.dts
@@ -169,6 +169,15 @@
 			reusable;
 			linux,cma-default;
 		};
+
+		ramoops@c00000000 {
+			compatible = "ramoops";
+			reg = <0xc 0x00000000 0x0 0x200000>;
+			no-map;
+			console-size = <0x100000>;
+			record-size = <0x40000>;
+			ecc-size = <16>;
+		};
 	};
 
 	sound {
